🥇 1. forceConsistentCasingInFileNames (must-have)
Why it’s essential
Immediately catches case sensitivity mismatch between imports and actual file names
Prevents CI/Linux-only failures
Protects codebase integrity long term
Zero cost and always ON
Industry recommendation
Keep it always enabled in tsconfig.json
This is now considered a standard in TypeScript and large automation frameworks.
{
  "compilerOptions": {
    "forceConsistentCasingInFileNames": true
  }
}
🥇 2. tsc --noEmit before running tests
Why it’s important
Catches all compile/type errors before running Playwright
Ensures PR/CI pipeline quality
Prevents failing tests due to broken imports or types
In package.json:
"scripts": {
  "check-types": "tsc --noEmit",
  "test": "npm run check-types && playwright test"
}
This becomes part of your CI pipeline as a type gatekeeper.
